     "span": "मक्खियाँ, मच्छर और भँवरे",
     "evidence": "Tibetan lists three insects: སྦྲང་བུ (fly), ཤ་སྦྲང་ (flesh-fly / gadfly) and བུང་བ (bee). bo-kunpal 7-18 glosses them as སྦྲང་བུ 'flying in the sky', ཤ་ཡི་སྦྲང་བུ 'flesh-fly' and བུང་བ 'that drinks flower nectar'. 'मच्छर' (mosquito) is not in the Tibetan (it comes from Sanskrit maśaka, which the Tibetan does not render), and བུང་བ is a bee rather than a bumblebee/भँवरा; english_academic has 'flies, gadflies, and bees'.",
